      "title": "Radius Philosophy",
      "content": "The system deliberately splits into two radius families: SHARP (2px and 5px) for all content-bearing surfaces — cards, inputs, images, tiles — and EXTREME (160px, 800px, 1600px) for all interactive or status elements — buttons, badges, tags, icon frames. This 2px/1600px axis is a defining signature: the sharp tiles read as machine-precise content, while the pills read as hand-pushed, chunky, tactile. Never use mid-range radii like 8px or 12px — they dilute the contrast between the two families."
    },
