      "title": "Typography Compression",
      "content": "All display sizes (40px+) use line-heights below 1.0 (0.85–0.95). This is uncommon — most systems use lh 1.1–1.3 for headings. The compressed leading makes headlines feel stamped rather than set, and is paired with aggressive negative tracking that scales proportionally: -0.06em at 150px, -0.04em at 80px, -0.02em at 27px. When recreating this system, do not normalize line-heights to 1.0+ for large sizes — the compression is load-bearing."
